3. Model Compression Techniques

After training, we compress the model to fit edge devices.

---

A. Quantization

Original FP32 weights

0.23456789
-0.98765432
0.54321987

Each weight uses 32 bits.

---

Convert to INT8

24
-99
54

Each weight now uses only 8 bits.

Benefits

Before| After
100 MB| 25 MB
High RAM| Low RAM
Slow| Faster

Advantages:

- 4× smaller models
- Lower memory usage
- Faster inference
- Reduced power consumption

---

Types of Quantization

Post-Training Quantization (PTQ)

Train Model
     ↓
Convert to INT8

Advantages:

- Fast
- Easy

Disadvantage:

- Slight accuracy drop

---

Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)

Train while simulating INT8 errors
            ↓
Export INT8 model

Advantages:

- Preserves accuracy
- Best choice for edge deployment

---

B. Pruning

Many weights contribute almost nothing:

0.00001
0.000003
-0.000005

These weights can be removed.

100 Million Parameters
           ↓
40 Million Parameters

Advantages:

- Smaller models
- Faster execution
- Less memory usage

